      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Oral Mydocalm intermittent therapy was used in 113 patients suffering from myogenous cephalalgia. Daily 3 +/- 150 mg tolperisonum doses relieved, within 3-7 days, spasm, hypertonicity, rigidity of occipital, cervical, and shoulder muscles, and resulted in functional improvement and successfully controlled myogenous cephalalgias."},
